<title>FRANCE: Dexia denies eying Depfa Bank stake.</title>
<headline>Dexia denies eying Depfa Bank stake.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Franco-belgian banking group Dexia issued a statement on Friday denying what it said were rumours that it was eying a stake in Depfa Bank of Germany.</p>
<p>&quot;Dexia denies all plans of that sort. It is not considering becoming a shareholder, at any level, of Depfa Bank,&quot; it said in the statement. It did not say where it had heard such rumours and there had been no prominent newspaper reports alluding to such move.</p>
<p>Credit Communal de Belgique (CCB) and Credit Local de France together form Dexia, a group mainly active in public sector lending.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
